    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nIn cases like working with a Java codebase, there are directory that contain another directory and nothing else. For example,\n\n* `com/` only contains `google/`\n* which only contains `search/`\n* which only contains `team_name/`\n* which only contains `application_name/` which contains all the source code for an app\n\nUsing mini.files, I often have to enter each directory individually. I'd like the option to configure the plugin to combine such cases of nesting into a single entry in the mini.files UI. In the case above, I'd see `com/google/search/team_name/application_name`. Pressing enter on that entry would take me directly to the `application_name` directory.\n\nA slight drawback to this feature: this feature would mean that we'd have to have a way to also enter the `com/` without skipping all the way to `application_name` since there is the (minority) case where we don't want to skip.\n\nThere is a bit of thought needed on the exact design/implementation of this feature, but I think this idea would make mini.files more ergonomic for the common use case.",
